speechtext:
1.	The government's policy with respect to the awarding of 'consulting and professional services' is set out in the Treasury Board's Administrative Manual, Chapter 315, which provides departments with the procedures appropriate for specific circumstances.
(a)	These procedures are:
(i)	"selection without competition"-only one firm is considered; for use in specified exceptional circumstances;
(ii)	"selection by qualifications"-contract is negotiated with firm or individual considered best qualified; used when proposals are not warranted;
(iii)	"design competition"-prizes are awarded for firm or firms submitting best designs, and contract is negotiated for design and related work; used for major works of national significance, for design and build projects, or as the first phase of a product development competition;
(iv)	"selection based on proposals excluding price data"- proposals are invited from a limited number of consultants on a short list; used where the work can be only broadly defined, the detailed work requirements are to be identified by the selected consultant, and the cost cannot be reliably estimated;
(v)	"selection based on proposals including cost data"- similar to (iv) except for the provision of cost data as basis for price negotiations; used where costs can be estimated reliably;
(vi)	"selection based on proposals including price"-similar to (iv) and (v) except that a price is offered; used when an accurate estimate of the costs is possible;
(vii)	"selection based on price offered"-selection of qualified consultant based on best price and fully compliant offer; used when the work can be specified precisely, the cost can be estimated reliably, more than one firm is capable and interested, and work acceptance criteria can be clearly specified.
(b)	Not applicable.
2.	Yes, see answer above.
